//CTP Editor Structure file
//For more detailed comments see advance.ces

0.3 //Version number

#%047%047	//Comment charachter in data file
%032%009	//Delimiter charachters in data file
		// (use %nnn for ASCII ref)
:		//Break on right quasi-delimiter
}{		//Break on left quasi-delimiter

1 //Format

f //Whether this has a number at the top (num of entries)
f //Whether this has a tree structure
t //Whether this file references GL entries
t //Whether this file has entries in gl_str.txt
t //Whether the entries have an article
f //Whether this file is the GL icon file
f //Whether this structure file describes formatting of fields
  // (i.e. whether it has the LBF and LAF columns below)

//Name			Comp	PByDef	AMult	NumArgs
	//Type		DefaultValue	Comment
DefaultIcon		t	t	f	1
	uniticon.ces	ICON_%n		Icon ID for this Government. Must be a valid Icon ID from UnitIcon.txt
Description		t	t	f	1
	0		DESCRIPTION_WONDER_ARISTOTLES_LYCEUM	Not used, but must be a valid string ID
Movie			t	t	f	1
	0		MOVIE_WONDER_	Wonder movie
EnableAdvance		f	t	f	1
	advance.ces	ADVANCE_	Advance ID that enables this government. Must be a valid Advance ID from Advance.txt
ObsoleteAdvance		f	f	f	1
	advance.ces	ADVANCE_	Advance ID that obsoletes this government. Up to 5 Obsolete Advances can be defined. Must be a valid Advance ID from Advance.txt
ProductionCost		t	t	f	1
	0		2000		Cost to build
ReduceReadinessCost	f	f	f	1
	0		25		Percent reduction in readiness costs
DecCrimePercent		f	f	f	1
	0		30		Percent reduction in crime
IncKnowledgePercent	f	f	f	1
	0		20		Percent increase in science
DecEmpireSize		f	f	f	1
	0		100		Percent reduction to empire size unhappiness
IncHappinessEmpire	f	f	f	1
	0		2		Amount to increase happiness in owners cities
IncConvertedCitiesFeePercent	f	f	f	1
	0		0		Comment
GoldPerWaterTradeRoute	f	f	f	1
	0		15		Gold per trade route of another empire crossing a water tile
GoldPerTelevision	f	f	f	1
	0		15		Gold per opponent-controlled television (Buildings with Television flag)
GoldPerInternationalTradeRoute	f	f	f	1
	0		25		Gold per trade route between two other empires
PollutersToParks	f	f	f	1
	0		3		Number of most polluting cities to destroy as if by CreatePark
ReduceWorldPollution	f	f	f	1
	0		0		Comment
IncreaseBoatMovement	f	f	f	1
	0		100		Increase to movement of owners boats
DecreaseMaintenance	f	f	f	1
	0		0		Comment
RandomAdvanceChance	f	f	f	1
	0		0		Comment
IncreaseHp		f	f	f	1
	0		0		Increases HP of owners units
MultiplyTradeRoutes	f	f	f	1
	0		0		Comment
IncreaseScientists	f	f	f	1
	0		5		?
OtherCivRandomAdvanceChance	f	f	f	1
	0		0		Comment
IncreaseProduction	f	f	f	1
	0		10		Percent production increase
BonusGold		f	f	f	1
	0		100		?
IncreaseFoodAllCities	f	f	f	1
	0		30		Percent increase to food in owners cities
TemporaryFullHappiness	f	f	f	1
	0		5		Turns of celebration in owners cities
IncreaseSpecialists	f	f	f	1
	0		0		Comment
IncreaseCathedrals	f	f	f	1
	0		0		Comment
IncreaseBrokerages	f	f	f	1
	0		50		Percent improvement to buildings with Brokerage flag
IncreaseRegard		f	f	f	1
	0		100		Improves other civs regard of the owner
BuildingEverywhere	f	f	f	1
	buildings.ces	IMPROVE_	Puts this building in every city. The building can still be built, and the effect remains once the wonder is obsolete.
PollutionPercent	f	f	f	1
	0		0		Comment
PollutionAmount		f	f	f	1
	0		0		Comment
EmbassiesEverywhere	f	f	f	0	Owner gets embassies with all civs except those at war with owner
CloseEmbassies		f	f	f	0	Close other civs embassies with owner
ReformCities		f	f	f	0	Reforms all cities for free
FreeSlaves		f	f	f	0	Flees all slaves in all civs, causing unhappiness in civs other than owners
GlobalRadar		f	f	f	0	Reveals map
SpiesEverywhere		f	f	f	0	Protects from enemy espionage as if spy in every city
ProtectFromBiologicalWarfare	f	f	f	0	Protects from enemy biological warfare attacks
EnableParkRangers	f	f	f	0	Allows construction of park rangers (presumably all units with CreateParks ability) for all civs
AllCitizensContent	f	f	f	0	Sets happiness in all cities to content (75?)
EliminateNukes		f	f	f	0	Removes nukes and prevents their construction
AllBoatsDeepWater	f	f	f	0	Gives MovementType: Sea to all units with MovementType: ShallowWater
ForcefieldEverywhere	f	f	f	0	Probably obsolete - better to use BuildingEverywhere
RevoltingCitiesJoinPlayer	f	f	f	0	Cities of other civs which revolt join owner
NoPollutionUnhappiness	f	f	f	0	Removes all pollution unhappiness
EmbassiesEverywhereEvenAtWar	f	f	f	0	Owner gets embassies with all civs
PreventConversion	f	f	f	0	Prevents cleric conversion of owners cities
ProtectFromBarbarians	f	f	f	0	?
StartGaiaController	f	f	f	0	Allows end game process
FreeTradeRoutes		f	f	f	0	? Probably doesn't work - try it
GLHidden		f	f	f	0	Removes GL entry for this entry
@ //End of fields

DefaultIcon      //The field which references the GL icon entry in uniticon.txt
DATABASE_WONDERS //Name of database for GL hyperlinks
WONDER_          //The prefix which identifies this file in gl_str.txt
_ARTICLE         //The article suffix